[#:seon.task{:name "an-agent-cannot-see-or-choose-its-change"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(my.program/overrides {}) answers [] on a branch with 21 changed identities; propose-merge! takes only :seon.issue/id, sweeps in drift the branch inherits (my.plan-test/current-refuses-an-unknown-agent-by-name), omits deletions from :seon.test/changed, and sends its content as a pr-str string. Selection exists only in root's prepare-merge!."
             :must-read #{my.program/overrides my.program/propose-merge!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-author-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-report-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "breaks-plans-a-contract-change-as-a-retraction"
             :kind :function
             :intent "breaks for a contract change takes the contract only as a string, titles every plan issue 'must be repaired before retracting', lists the subject as its own caller, and never states the arity mismatch (call sites show the old arity only); the install gate does not consult it for an arity-changing redefinition."
             :must-read #{my.program/breaks}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-maintainer-opus-2026-09-26.md"
                         "docs/seon/issues/breaks-for-a-contract-change-plans-a-retraction.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "breaks-costs-seconds-on-a-hub"
             :kind :function
             :intent "my.program/breaks takes 7.8 s on a hub (seon.db/q, armed): proposed-plan -> gate-sets with ~2M datom calls; ns-unmap! inherits it. Selection must follow call reach per the owner ruling and stay sub-second."
             :must-read #{my.program/breaks}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/docs-exploration-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-one-line-change-resends-the-whole-definition"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "There is no REPL entrance to change part of an existing definition: to add one map entry to seon.render.value/tree the agent resent the whole 38-line defn (about 1,200 tokens) each attempt, and the whole 45-line mcp-get-value (about 1,300 tokens) to change one contract keyword, where a file edit sends one line. my.edit edits files, not program entities. An entrance that takes the stored declaration, applies a form-level replacement and evaluates the result as the defn would make the REPL cheaper than the file for the common edit."
             :must-read #{my.program/history my.edit/form!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "propose-refusal-names-no-next-step"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(my.program/propose-merge! {}) on an unassigned branch answers the bare string \"seon.task is refused: unassigned.\" (the declared renderer shows only the message): no offending branch/agent, no fix naming who assigns (root's seon.task/assign!) or how a file task in resources/seon/tasks becomes assignable. An agent also has no my.* entrance to create its own branch (MCP's branch tool has none for Seon agents). The refusal names its assignment query and the call that fixes it."
             :must-read #{my.program/propose-merge! seon.task/assignment seon.task/assign!}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-merged-change-reaching-the-files-is-unproven"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The last unproven step of the dogfood path: an agent's merged change reaches the files through write-back (my.program/write-back!). Done when a live branch change is proposed, merged and written back, the file diff equals the change, and the run is recorded as evidence (tmp/repl-audit/change.md lists the prior gaps)."
             :must-read #{my.program/prepare-merge! my.program/write-back!}
             :evidence #{"tmp/repl-audit/change.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "history-shows-the-source-twice-and-no-commit-id"
             :kind :function
             :intent "my.program/history shows a definition's source twice per event and the write-back transaction carries no commit id. Done when each history event names the commit id recorded on its write-back transaction and shows a diff render instead of the second source copy."
             :must-read #{my.program/declaration-diff my.program/history}
             :evidence #{"tmp/repl-audit/change.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "ns-unmap-and-remove-ns-cost-quarter-thousand-tokens-and-most-of-a-second"
             :kind :function
             :intent "my.program/ns-unmap! and remove-ns! add about 250 tokens of constant prose to every reply and take 0.6-0.8 s. Done when a reply is the value and one line, and the call is under 300 ms, timed against the same probe on the parent commit."
             :must-read #{my.program/ns-unmap! my.program/remove-ns!}
             :evidence #{"tmp/repl-audit/change.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-merge-prepare-costs-three-seconds-and-400k-calls"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The merge path: my.program/prepare-merge! takes 2.6-3.1 s and about 400k calls regardless of change size. The cold-projection hypothesis was falsified (800a94abb); it needs a sampled profile (Astra after a bow-out), then the responsible armed functions named and fixed. Done when a small merge prepares under one second, timed on parent and change."
             :must-read #{my.program/prepare-merge! seon.cluster.source/prepare-merge!}}
 #:seon.task{:name "source-repeats-the-docstring",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "source-display/printer-notes.md reports my.program/source returns the docstring both inside source and separately as doc. Return source plus only useful nonduplicated data or improve its declared render; keep value printer schema-agnostic. Regression at my.program/source/render's data boundary.",
            :evidence
            #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-07/source-display/review-printer-codex-notes.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "alias-and-require-as-retarget-silently"
  :kind :function
  :intent "In SCI, (require '[clojure.set :as x]) after x -> clojure.string returns nil and retargets the alias; so does (alias 'x 'clojure.walk) (sci-alias is a bare assoc-in, namespaces.cljc:478-486). Clojure refuses a different target (Namespace.java:257-258, \"Alias x already exists in namespace .., aliasing ..\"). The silent retarget makes stored definitions position-dependent and is the source of the digest refusals in the alias design probes. Correct: alias and require :as with a different target refuse as Clojure does, ns-unalias! being the guarded path (SCI runs ns-unalias itself); a refer replacement stays legal (a warning in Clojure). Related issue docs/seon/issues/reload-refuses-an-alias-retargeted-by-the-new-source.md. Proof: evaluating (alias 'x 'clojure.set) after x -> clojure.string answers a refusal error and leaves the alias unchanged."
  :must-read #{my.program/ns-unalias!}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/s5-admission/alias-design.md" "docs/seon/issues/reload-refuses-an-alias-retargeted-by-the-new-source.md"}}]
